  "description": "E1-L: where a scene transition sits on the timeline. The gateway (scene-transition-timing.ts) and the editor (youtorch-ui/lib/spark/scene-transitions.ts) plan the same windows from the same inputs; both read this file (a byte-identical copy guarded by a digest on each side). `plans` is keyed by the INCOMING scene id and lists only scenes that store a transition_in. Timeline v3: `animation_holds` pins what a transition does to the scenes' own animations inside its window (gateway scene-transition-animations.ts, editor stage/transition-animation-hold.ts): `side` from = the outgoing scene (exit animations, held at the window start `frame`), to = the incoming scene (entry animations, held at the window end `frame`); `roles` names the animations; `expected` are the tracks after the hold.",
